From: Rob Lymm <rob@mediaeden.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: look for a hang when the GPU says it has one

On A3XX the hardware has its own interface hang detector. With it enabled,
an Adreno 330 reports a stall several seconds before the hangcheck timer
notices, and reports stalls that clear by themselves: in one 48 second test
the hardware raised seven, while the timer declared three lockups eighteen
seconds after the first report.

Waiting that long matters twice over. The screen stays frozen, and the GPU
state captured for diagnosis is taken long after whatever went wrong, so it
no longer describes the fault.

Add msm_gpu_hangcheck_soon(), which brings a pending hangcheck forward
without changing what it decides: if the submission has retired, or the
command processor has moved since the last look, nothing happens. Call it
from the A3XX handler when the hang detect interrupt arrives.

diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-09-20 08:26:07.878692232 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-09-20 08:25:45.589689273 +0100
@@ -451,6 +451,14 @@
 
 	if (status & A3XX_INT0_RBBM_AHB_ERROR)
 		gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_AHB_CMD, BIT(3));
+
+	/*
+	 * The GPU's own interface hang detector fires seconds before the
+	 * hangcheck timer would notice, and fires for stalls that clear by
+	 * themselves. Ask the timer to look now; it still decides.
+	 */
+	if (status & A3XX_INT0_MISC_HANG_DETECT)
+		msm_gpu_hangcheck_soon(gpu);
 }
 
 static irqreturn_t a3xx_irq(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c	2026-09-20 08:25:16.421369699 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c	2026-09-20 08:25:45.589247969 +0100
@@ -503,6 +503,17 @@
 			round_jiffies_up(jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(priv->hangcheck_period)));
 }
 
+/*
+ * Look for a hang now rather than at the next tick, for hardware that reports
+ * a stall itself. The timer's own decision is unchanged: if work has retired
+ * or the command processor has moved on since the last look, nothing happens.
+ */
+void msm_gpu_hangcheck_soon(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
+{
+	if (timer_pending(&gpu->hangcheck_timer))
+		mod_timer(&gpu->hangcheck_timer, jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(20));
+}
+
 static bool made_progress(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct msm_ringbuffer *ring)
 {
 	if (ring->hangcheck_progress_retries >= DRM_MSM_HANGCHECK_PROGRESS_RETRIES)
diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h	2026-09-20 08:25:17.293369845 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h	2026-09-20 08:25:45.589488977 +0100
@@ -650,6 +650,7 @@
 		uint32_t *totaltime, uint32_t ncntrs, uint32_t *cntrs);
 
 void msm_gpu_retire(struct msm_gpu *gpu);
+void msm_gpu_hangcheck_soon(struct msm_gpu *gpu);
 void msm_gpu_submit(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct msm_gem_submit *submit);
 
 int msm_gpu_init(struct drm_device *drm, struct platform_device *pdev,
